        <div class="section" id="intro">
            <h2><span class="section-icon">📘</span>Introduction</h2>
<div class="objectifs">
<h4>Objectives</h4>
<ul>
<li>Establish the equivalent circuit of a line, a cable and a transformer from manufacturer data.</li>
<li>Convert physical quantities to per-unit quantities and back.</li>
<li>Calculate a voltage drop and losses; check a voltage profile.</li>
<li>Write the load-flow equations, do one Gauss-Seidel iteration by hand and interpret the convergence of the three methods.</li>
<li>Calculate three-phase, phase-to-phase and phase-to-earth short-circuit currents according to IEC 60909 and deduce the breaking capacity.</li>
</ul>
<p class="prereq">Prerequisites: level 1, elementary matrix calculus. Duration: 20 to 25 h.</p>
</div>

