<h3>Contribution of induction motors to the short circuit</h3>
<p>During the first cycles of a fault, the rotor flux of an induction motor maintains an emf: the motor feeds into the fault a current close
to its starting current, which dies out within a few cycles. IEC 60909 represents it by the impedance
<i>Z</i><sub>M</sub> = <i>U</i><sub>n</sub>²/(<i>I</i><sub>LR</sub>/<i>I</i><sub>rM</sub> · <i>S</i><sub>rM</sub>) (positive and negative sequences;
no zero-sequence path), with <i>R</i>/<i>X</i> = 0.10 (MV motors of at least 1 MW), 0.15 (MV under 1 MW) or 0.42 (LV, cables included); it
increases I"k and ip but is neglected for the minimum current. In NRJXpert, <i>I</i><sub>LR</sub>/<i>I</i><sub>rM</sub> is taken from the
equivalent circuit of the machine (<i>s</i> = 1).</p>
<div class="ex"><h4>Example 2.13 — Three-phase fault at the bus of a 2 MVA motor</h4>
<p>With the network of example 5.5 (file <code>exemples/demarrage_moteur.xml</code>, « Short circuit » calculation), three-phase fault at the
motor bus, maximum Icc. <i>I</i><sub>LR</sub>/<i>I</i><sub>rM</sub> = 6.14; <i>U</i><sub>n</sub> = 6 kV.</p>
<details class="sol"><summary>Show the solution</summary>
<p>Network: |<i>Z</i>| = |0.07 + j0.96| = 0.9625 Ω, I"k = 1.1 × 6 000/(√3 × 0.9625) = <span class="result">3 959 A</span>.
Motor: |<i>Z</i><sub>M</sub>| = 6²/(6.14 × 2) = 2.93 Ω (<i>R</i>/<i>X</i> = 0.10), I"kM = 1.1 × 6 000/(√3 × 2.93) =
<span class="result">1 300 A</span>. Total (sum nearly in phase): <span class="result">5 259 A</span>, i.e. +33 %; κ goes from 1.81 to 1.79
and ip from 10.1 to 13.3 kA. The breaking capacity and the withstand of the busbars must take it into account.</p>
</details></div>

